{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1764601,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"IG:NITE","festival_id":520881,"organization_id":943045,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-01T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-22T16:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/ignite-bharati-vidyapeeths-college-of-engineering-1764601","region":"hybrid","details":"<p><strong>Overview:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>IG:NITE<\/strong> is a premier technical competition organized under BVEST XIII by BVP-ISTE &times; GeeksforGeeks Campus Body, BVCOE. Moving away from disposable, built-from-scratch hackathon prototypes, IG:NITE focuses on <strong>project revival and evolution<\/strong>. Teams are challenged to bring a genuine existing codebase&mdash;whether from a past hackathon, academic work, startup, or personal project&mdash;and build a major, bespoke feature on top of it.<\/p>\n<p>The competition encourages participants to align their projects and newly developed features with the <strong>UN Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)<\/strong>, such as SDG 4 (Quality Education), SDG 8 (Decent Work &amp; Economic Growth), SDG 9 (Industry, Innovation &amp; Infrastructure), SDG 11 (Sustainable Cities), SDG 12 (Responsible Consumption), and SDG 17 (Partnerships for the Goals).<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round-wise Details:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Online Project Screening<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Format: Online code &amp; project evaluation.<\/li>\n<li>Mechanism: Teams submit their best existing project during registration. Submissions are screened based on technical depth, code originality, system architecture, execution quality, creativity, and growth potential.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2: Offline Project Revival<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Location: Offline Campus Sprint &amp; Live Defense.<\/li>\n<li>Stage 1 (Bespoke Challenge): Shortlisted teams receive a custom-tailored feature challenge engineered specifically around their submitted project's tech stack and codebase.<\/li>\n<li>Stage 2 (Development Sprint): Teams undergo an offline development sprint to implement, integrate, and test the assigned feature within the allocated timeframe.<\/li>\n<li>Stage 3 (Live Demo &amp; Defense): Teams present their original project alongside the newly integrated custom feature in a live demonstration and technical defense before a panel of judges.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules and Guidelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Eligibility: Open to undergraduate (Bachelor's) and postgraduate (Master's) students across all disciplines.<\/li>\n<li>Project Authenticity: Submitted projects must represent original, genuine work by the team. Purely cloned or plagiarized codebases will be disqualified.<\/li>\n<li>Codebase Constraint: Shortlisted teams <strong>must<\/strong> build upon the exact codebase submitted during Round 1. Building a completely new project during Round 2 is strictly prohibited.<\/li>\n<li>Custom Feature Execution: Teams must strictly adhere to the bespoke feature challenge assigned to them by the organizers.<\/li>\n<li>SDG &amp; Impact Integration: Teams are encouraged to highlight real-world applicability, scalability, technological sustainability, and relevant UN SDG alignments during their live defense.<\/li>\n<li>Judges' Authority: The decisions made by the judges and organizing committee across all stages are final and non-contestable.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Evaluation &amp; Weightage Breakdown:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Custom Feature Implementation (60% Weightage):\n<ul>\n<li>Technical Implementation &amp; Functionality<\/li>\n<li>Integration with Existing Codebase<\/li>\n<li>Innovation, Code Quality &amp; Modularity<\/li>\n<li>Execution &amp; Delivery within the Sprint Timeframe<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Original Project Depth (40% Weightage):\n<ul>\n<li>Originality &amp; Technical Maturity<\/li>\n<li>System Architecture &amp; Complexity<\/li>\n<li>User Experience, Completeness &amp; Stability<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><em>(Note: Specialized judging criteria may be introduced for domain-specific projects such as AI\/ML, Web3, or Distributed Cloud Systems.)<\/em><\/p>\n<div id=\"model-response-message-contentr_4b742ac54bdb9a69\" class=\"markdown markdown-main-panel md-content enable-luminous-fast-follows enable-updated-hr-color stronger tutor-markdown-rendering\" dir=\"ltr\" aria-busy=\"false\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n<div><strong data-path-to-node=\"0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Contact for Queries<\/strong><\/div>\n<br \/>\n<ul>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"1\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Nikhil Shrivastava<\/strong> &mdash; +91 81781 86964<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"2\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Shubh Narang<\/strong> &mdash; +91 87508 97605<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":33478161,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-01T23:20:27+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-05T09:36:33+05:30","communication_sent":1,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"dk1In0r","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":0,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":null,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":16,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-10-02 11:06:00","auto_shortlist_trigger":false,"enable_ai_discussion":false,"total_unlock_teams":0,"enable_hiring_automation":false,"auto_send_participation_certificate":true,"closed_at":null,"linkedInEventId":"","teams":[],"players":[],"logoUrl":"https:\/\/d8it4huxumps7.